# Harness-lab core rules

Read `AGENTS.md` at session start. It is the router — do not load every doc into context upfront.

## Workflow

1. Run `bash scripts/init.sh` before coding
2. Work from `specs/SPECS.md` — one logical unit per session
3. Run `bash scripts/verify.sh` before commit
4. Blockers → `state/blocked.md`, then stop

## When the agent errs

Update the harness (rules, docs, specs), not only the code. Same mistake twice = missing instruction.

## Docs

Point at file paths; do not duplicate code behavior in markdown.

## Commits

Detailed messages: what changed, why, how verified.

## Research

Use subagents/helpers for exploration only — implementation stays in the main session with full harness context.
